BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Write Now! with Mark Sanford Gross
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T170000
UID:260827Zj_a0K27tE2OrJb3NaKNqQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Write Now!\, a new writing group led by local writ
 ing coach Mark Sanford Gross. \n\nWrite Now! is an in-the-moment program 
 for all folks who want to explore free writing\, story-telling\, and curio
 sity about what happens when you get a notebook\, pen\, and a nudge. Share
  the beauty of 'the spoken word' with others in this enthusiastic communit
 y-building event through writing in a non-judgemental and trusting atmosph
 ere. Bring friends and family.\n\nMark Sanford Gross has been building com
 munity through writing for the past few years along our coast.  He is the
  Creator and Co-Host of the local radio station's weekly program KGUA-Writ
 ers. He hosts writing workshops for local schools\, recovery programs at M
 endonoma Health Alliance\, and local pop-up destinations.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wild Berry Picking Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T160000
UID:26082756Dy_djNWkWl9ILA5oxFuw
DESCRIPTION:Explore the diverse landscapes of The Sea Ranch Lodge Farm on 
 a guided 1.5-mile hike through riparian forests\, open rangelands\, and sc
 enic silvopasture. Along the way\, enjoy sweeping coastal views and season
 al huckleberry picking while learning about the farm and surrounding lands
 cape.\n\nThe trail follows historic logging roads with a 400-foot elevatio
 n gain before descending back to the farm. Please wear sturdy shoes and br
 ing water. Steep sections may be challenging for guests with limited mobil
 ity. Dogs are not permitted.\n\nFamilies are welcome\, though the hike may
  be challenging for some children.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:https://www.thesearanchlodge.com/programming/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
