DESCRIPTION:Discover the creative art of linocut printmaking with Bay Area
  artist Ana Bianchi in this hands-on workshop designed for beginners and c
 urious makers alike.\n\nYou’ll learn the fundamentals of stamp carving a
 nd relief printing while exploring pattern\, imagery\, and repeatable desi
 gn through playful experimentation. Beginning with an easy-to-carve white 
 eraser before progressing to professional rubber carving blocks\, particip
 ants will gain confidence using carving tools\, safely handling materials\
 , and understanding the unique reverse-image process of printmaking.\n\nSa
 turday\, September 5\, 10:30 a.m. – 1:30 p.m.\n\n$78 for members\, $95 f
 or non-members | Includes Garden admission. Please check in at the Center 
 for Learning & Engagement. To learn more and sign up\, click “Register
 ” and explore the “Info” tab on the registration page.\n\n**Please n
 ote that a $10 materials fee is required for this workshop and is not in
 cluded in the registration price.** Participants should bring $10 cash\, p
 ayable directly to the artist on the day of the workshop. Material kits wi
 ll be available upon arrival and include all of the tools and supplies n
 eeded for the class\, so no additional materials are required.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
