BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Entre Bosques y Lagos – Una Caminata en Espanol
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T133000
UID:260803xygRca9sHEeirIj4niX8oQ
DESCRIPTION:Acompáñanos en una caminata guiada en el bosque de Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park. Vamos a empezar por explorar la comunidad abandona
 da del Sonoma Developmental Center y de ahi iremos por el paisaje montaño
 so rumbo a Fern Lake\, caminaremos hasta el área del Huerto y regresaremo
 s rodeando el lago. Esta caminata es ideal para quienes disfrutan de la na
 turaleza\, el aire fresco y las vistas tranquilas del bosque.  Es una exp
 eriencia educativa y interesante\, diseñada para conectar con la naturale
 za a un buen ritmo.\n\nAmong Forests and Lakes: Join a five-mile guided hi
 ke in Spanish through the woods at Jack London State Historic Park. Begin 
 by exploring the abandoned Sonoma Developmental Center grounds\, then head
  through the hilly landscape toward Fern Lake\, hike to the Orchard area\,
  and return by circling the lake. This hike is perfect for those who enjoy
  nature\, fresh air\, and peaceful forest views. It is an engaging\, educa
 tional experience designed to help connect with nature at a comfortable pa
 ce.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/bosquesylagos/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T170000
UID:260803vazyYlSn4kCEQBrQvxugJw
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T193000
UID:260803gaAX4LDLPEuFZcP-5R93Fw
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare (after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s n
 ame). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to questi
 on it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the cash\,
  tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate–l
 ie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drops in
 to many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that res
 onates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six act
 ors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of Shake
 speare's other plays-in-progress (one of which becomes the famous Macbeth.
 )
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intuitive Construction in Clay with Resident Gabriel Poucher
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T130000
UID:260803VNJoVfCDiE-hL4oEmXPEkw
DESCRIPTION:Fridays Weekly · 8 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 7 – Septe
 mber 25\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics 
 Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nA
 ll Levels\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$295\n\nExplore paperc
 lay\, handbuilding\, and multi-firing techniques to create small-to-medium
  sculptures – methods adaptable to any scale or artistic style.\n\nprogr
 am overview\n\nStudents will work with a variety of techniques and materia
 ls\, including paperclay\, nontraditional approaches to handbuilding\, and
  constructing sculptures over multiple firings. The class will focus on sm
 all to medium sculptural work\, but these techniques are applicable to any
  scale and genre.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/intuitive-construction-in-c
 lay/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
