BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260905T000000
UID:260606IsHZrhDJ4Ey1jlaJxuc6kw
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Original Certified Farmers Market is a year-rou
 nd Saturday tradition in Sonoma County\, bringing together local farmers\,
  ranchers\, food artisans\, and neighbors from 8:30 a.m. to 1 p.m. This is
  not just a place to shop\, it's a place to connect directly with the peop
 le who grow your food. As a Slow Food Sonoma County award recipient\, the 
 market prioritizes integrity\, seasonality\, and true farm-to-community re
 lationships. Expect peak-season produce harvested just hours before market
 \, pasture-raised meats\, fresh flowers\, artisan breads\, handcrafted goo
 ds\, and thoughtfully prepared foods that reflect the region's agricultura
 l richness. Visitors can stroll the vibrant open-air market\, sample local
  flavors\, and experience Sonoma County's food culture in its most authent
 ic form. Families\, chefs\, and weekend explorers alike gather here to dis
 cover what's growing now and to support small farms that keep our local fo
 od system strong. Open every Saturday\, rain or shine\, the Santa Rosa Ori
 ginal Certified Farmers Market is a cornerstone of the community and a mus
 t-visit stop for anyone wanting to taste\, shop\, and experience Sonoma Co
 unty at its freshest.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/#jlupcoming-events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tomales Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260906T170000
UID:260826SFddUOLqP06BEQJvPBG1Aw
DESCRIPTION:The **Tomales Festival** will be held at High Noon on Labor Da
 y Sunday\, September 6th. Join us in the Community Park (in between the Ca
 tholic church and the William Tell House) to celebrate with friends and ne
 ighbors. This year we're featuring music by the Blues Defenders\, plus fre
 sh oysters\, beer\, wine\, food\, and drink. Local arts and crafts\, plus 
 displays from local organizations and non-profits.\n\nThe festival is (and
  always has been) created\, organized\, and carried out by volunteers from
  the local community. This local tradition has quite a history: it was the
  Swiss-Italian celebration from 1888 until 1994\, when it became Founder's
  Day and later the Tomales Festival. That's 138 years worth of parades\, p
 icnics\, and parties. This event benefits the Tomales Town Hall\, which is
  a 501(c)3 non-profit community center.\n\nSpecial thanks to **Kathryn LeM
 ieux** for once again allowing us to use her whimsical cow painting as our
  festive logo. And thanks to our contributors. The **Hog Island Oyster Com
 pany** and **The Marshall Store** contributed the shellfish. **Morris Dist
 ributing** is providing our beer supply. **Recology Sonoma/Marin** is prov
 iding trash containers and is donating garbage service. We are grateful to
  our sponsor **Marin Agricultural Land Trust (MALT)**.\n\nSign ups for vo
 lunteers\, exhibitors\, vendors\, and more right are currently available. 
 Write to festival@TomalesTownHall.org or see the website: https://www.toma
 lestownhall.org/tomalesfest. Booth reservations end **August 15th**.
LOCATION:Tomales Community Park
URL:https://www.tomalestownhall.org/tomalesfest
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
