BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cosmos and Coco
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T220000
UID:260514agwaTyHxLk2ufgr8Vxb_Ag
DESCRIPTION:Begin your evening with a guided hike along our Planet Walk Tr
 ail\, a flat and scenic journey to Saturn and back\, approximately 1.2 mil
 es in total\, beneath the darkening sky as knowledgeable docents offer ins
 ightful facts at each planetary stop. Did you know: each step in our plane
 t walk is equivalent to 2.3 million miles through our solar system! After
  the walk\, return to the Robert Ferguson Observatory to warm up with a cu
 p of hot cocoa and an in-depth stargazing session led by one of our experi
 enced astronomers. The night sky tour blends science and storytelling\, he
 lping you appreciate the night sky in a whole new way.Once the Star guide 
 portion concludes\, guests are welcome to refill their cocoa and continue 
 observing through our telescopes for the remainder of the night. This pro
 gram is designed for families and guests of all ages who can comfortably e
 njoy a light hike and remain respectful and attentive while volunteers off
 er information. Please wear appropriate footwear and bring a white-light f
 lashlight for this event only.
LOCATION:Robert Ferguson Observatory
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/cosmos-cocoa-2026-tickets-240974
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thursday Night Live at Priest Ranch | Yountville
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T210000
UID:260504_l0h6eBCT0-mvMv4cows4Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our annual Thursday Night Live series—an ongoing
  celebration of great music\, good wine\, and easy Napa Valley evenings. T
 hroughout the season\, we’ll feature a rotating lineup of talented local
  and regional artists spanning a variety of genres.\n\nAdmission is compli
 mentary\, and seating is first-come\, first-served—so come early\, grab 
 your spot\, and settle in for the night. Enjoy your favorite Priest Ranch 
 wines available by the glass or bottle\, along with a special menu from Th
 e Kitchen crafted just for the occasion. Whether you’re winding down aft
 er work or gathering friends for a casual night out\, Thursday Night Live 
 is your standing invitation to sip\, savor\, and soak in the sounds.\n\nMu
 sic is complimentary. Wine and food are available to purchase. No reservat
 ion required.\n\n**July 9** — Carlos Ramirez Trio (Latin)\n\n**July 16**
  — David Ronconi Trio (Alternative)\n\n**July 23** — Sticky Bandits (C
 overs)\n\n**July 30** — Complicated Animals (Indie Nova)\n\n**August 6**
  — Radio Bobcat (Indie)\n\n**August 13** — Big Blu Soul Revue (Soul)\n
 \n**August 20** — Lilan Kane (Soul)\n\n**August 27** — Sean Carscaden 
 (Rock)\n\n**September 10** — Edgardo y Candela (Latin)\n\n**September 17
 ** — Steady Eddy & The Shakers (Motown)
LOCATION:Priest Ranch Tasting Room
URL:https://priestranchwines.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T193000
UID:260415724HCZoGdEaadpgWAniaFg
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T160000
UID:260312vGaiJRtw4UWAzLNLL0Ny9g
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Tasting Salon (Indoors Only)
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-brandlin-estate-win
 e-food-tasting-experience/18318441/2026-09-10T11
