UID:260820zXJj4ctjAEu_yu0JLUkZ3g
DESCRIPTION:Raised in the Bay Area\, DJ Cal has gained a reputation for do
 ing multi-genre set lists designed to move the crowds with a blend of Trap
 \, EDM\,Hip-Hop and Reggaeton music. He calls the city of Santa Rosa his h
 ome\, but you might’ve heard his mixes on-air across the nation \\(San F
 rancisco\, Las Vegas\, Orlando\, Palms Springs\, etc.\\). He currently hol
 ds a spot as a Mixshow DJ on Fresno California B95\, with Teezzy Radio\, L
 ast Call and Friday night street party. DJ CAL has several Bay Area and No
 rthern California venues under his belt and you can catch him performing a
 nd hanging out with the hottest names in music around the Bay. He also has
  created his own day party\, "Brunch Behavior" that has gained much popula
 rity in the North Bay. Also\, his work has been supported and featured by 
 various blogs\, websites and record pools\; DJ City\, MyMP3Pool\, BpmSupre
 me and SmashTheClub\, and more. DJ CAL has worked hard to make his own mar
 k in the music industry.
LOCATION:Perch + Plow
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108787165?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Benefit for Walker Creek Music Camp - An Evening of American Roots
  Music
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T210000
UID:260820QK0rL5cQEkOTFagM7DwzCA
DESCRIPTION:**Walker Creek Music Camp Presents Teacher Concert Series V**\
 n\n**Benefit Concert Celebrating American Roots Music**\n\n**SEBASTOPOL\, 
 CA** — Walker Creek Music Camp presents **Teacher Concert Series V** –
  **Benefit Concert** celebrating the rich traditions and exciting future o
 f American roots music on **Friday\, September 11\, 2026\, from 7:00–9:0
 0 p.m.** at the **Sebastopol Community Cultural Center**\, 390 Morris Stre
 et\, Sebastopol.\n\nProceeds from the concert support Walker Creek Music C
 amp’s mission to provide world-class music education and access to tradi
 tional American roots music for students of all ages. Audience members can
  look forward to an inspiring evening of live music featuring celebrated W
 CMC faculty alumni showcasing bluegrass\, old-time\, jazz\, swing and othe
 r forms of American roots music.\n\n**Performing artists: Crying Uncle Blu
 egrass Band – Evie Ladin Band – Pacific Drive**\n\n**Crying Uncle Blue
 grass Band –** Widely recognized as one of the most exciting young bands
  in acoustic music\, **Crying Uncle Bluegrass Band** blends bluegrass\, 
 Dawg music\, jazz\, and original compositions with remarkable musicianship
  and youthful energy. Brothers **Miles Quale** (mandolin\, guitar\, voca
 ls) and **Teo Quale** (fiddle\, guitar\, vocals) are joined by **Andrew
  Osborn** (bass\, vocals) and 2023 National Flat Pick Guitar Champion **
 Ian Ly** (guitar\, vocals)\, creating a fresh and innovative **sound root
 ed** in tradition.\n\nNamed the 2023 International Bluegrass Music Associ
 ation Momentum Band of the Year\, **the** group made its Grand Ole Opry 
 debut in 2024 and was honored to perform at the Bluegrass Music Hall of Fa
 me's induction of their musical hero\, David Grisman. Their performances h
 ave taken them to premier festivals across North America\, Europe\, and As
 ia\, earning a reputation as one of bluegrass music's brightest rising sta
 rs.\n\n*"Go and check out Crying Uncle! We dig what they are doing! The fu
 ture of music is in good hands here!*" — **David Grisman**\n\n**Evie La
 din Band –** Banjo player\, singer\, songwriter\, percussive dancer\, ch
 oreographer\, and square dance caller\, Evie Ladin is one of the most dy
 namic and innovative voices in contemporary roots music. Blending old-time
  Appalachian traditions with influences from African Diaspora music and da
 nce\, her performances are rich in rhythm\, storytelling\, and joyful ener
 gy.\n\nA master of clawhammer banjo\, Evie's music has been featured every
 where from *A Prairie Home Companion* and Lincoln Center to Hardly Stric
 tly Bluegrass and Celtic Connections. Based in Oakland\, California\, she 
 tours internationally with the **Evie Ladin Band**\, featuring **Keith T
 erry** (bass\, body percussion\, vocals) and **Erik Pearson** (guitar\,
  vocals). Together they create an exciting blend of old-time\, folk\, and 
 contemporary roots music. The band has released five acclaimed albums of o
 riginal "neo-traditional" music\, along with *Riding the Rooster*\, a col
 lection of traditional fiddle-banjo duets.\n\n"A natural entertainer with 
 a gift for infusing folk practices with contemporary verve." **– San Fra
 ncisco Chronicle**\n\n**Pacific Drive –** Pacific Drive was born at Walk
 er Creek Music Camp in 2015—at dances\, beside the pond\, and in late-ni
 ght jam sessions that stretched well past midnight.\n\nThe band features f
 iddler Dana Frankel\, mandolinist David Thiessen\, guitarist Jesse Fichman
  (formerly of AJ Lee & Blue Summit)\, bassist Helen Foley\, and banjoist S
 am Reed. Lifelong friends who grew up in California’s bluegrass communit
 y\, they deliver hard-driving traditional bluegrass\, tight harmonies\, an
 d the unmistakable chemistry of musicians who have played together since t
 heir teens.\n\n**About Walker Creek Music Camp –** Walker Creek Music Ca
 mp is a California nonprofit 501(c)(3) corporation (EIN 99-3474773) dedica
 ted to teaching\, preserving\, and celebrating American roots music tradit
 ions. Founded in 2013\, the camp welcomes students of all ages to experien
 ce its world-class music education program held twice each year at the Wal
 ker Creek Ranch Conference Center\, just west of Petaluma.\n\nWalker Creek
 ’s Music & More (M&M’s) youth program offers tuition-free instruction 
 for children ages 6–13\, and also provides scholarships and work-trade o
 pportunities that make music education accessible to all—ensuring that t
 raditional music continues to thrive for generations to come.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Community Cultural Center
URL:https://walkercreekmusiccamp.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:macbitches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T210000
UID:260820CFKClek8ekad3dyJGLF8wQ
DESCRIPTION:“macbitches takes Shakespearean themes and grounds them in 
 a recognizable\, modern reality — a smarter\, theater-centered Mean Gir
 ls\, if you will. It’s funny\, sharp\, and unafraid to let women be comp
 licated.” - Jeanette Seisdedos\, director\n\nmacbitches takes a darkly 
 funny look at the toxic\, high-stakes world of university theater\, center
 ing on a freshman who unexpectedly lands the role of Lady Macbeth. The pla
 y centers on freshman acting major Hailey\, who unexpectedly scores the co
 veted role of Lady Macbeth. Her upperclassmen rivals immediately invite he
 r over to “celebrate.” As the Fireball and Svedka flow\, the young wom
 en interrogate their own ambitions as well as the power structures that ha
 ve shaped their education—and when the night spirals into violent and sh
 ocking acts of betrayal\, they come to learn that what’s done cannot be 
 undone.\n\n\\*Content Advisory: Strong profanity\, physical and psycholog
 ical violence\, heavy substance abuse and underage drinking\, discussions 
 of mental illness and sexual misconduct\, and themes of betrayal and suici
 de. Recommended for mature audiences 16+.\n\nWritten by Sophie McIntosh\n\
 nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos\n\nRunning Time: 90 minutes with no interm
 ission\n\nSeptember 4th\, 5th\, 6th\, \\*10th\, 11th\, 12th\, 13th\, 18th\
 , 19th\, 20th.\n\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:30 PM\n\nSunday Matinee: 
 2:00 PM\n\n\\*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM\n\n Adults: $25\n\nStudent w/ID:
  $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performance:  Pay What You Can\n\nWri
 tten by Sophie McIntosh\n\nDirected by Jeanette Seisdedos
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/macbitches/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T180000
UID:260813wOZTtRxEFESdh6FT16OqTg
DESCRIPTION:EPTEMBER ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES\n\nDate: 
 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  8/12/26\n\nDATES: August 31 – September 27\, 20
 26\n\nRECEPTION:  SATURDAY\, September 5 – 3 -6 pm Join Donna Schaff
 er and Tosya Shore to celebrate the show and learn about their artistic i
 nspirations.  Refreshments will be served.  \n\nFeatured Artist Donna 
 Schaffer Celebrates Wine Country Beauty in “The Days of Vines and Roses
 ”\n\nSonoma County artist Donna Schaffer unveils her latest collection o
 f oil paintings\, “The Days of Vines and Roses\,” celebrating some of 
 her favorite views of roses blooming among the vineyards\, hills\, and woo
 dlands of Sonoma County. At the heart of the collection is Vines and Trell
 is of Roses\, where glorious pink roses spill across an entrance trellis\,
  set against the orderly rows of a vineyard. In Mini Red Roses Along Viney
 ard\, delicate red roses punctuate the landscape\, creating a lively inter
 play between vineyard rows\, stands of trees\, and the hills beyond. “Li
 ving here in Sonoma County for three decades\, I never tire of its gloriou
 s natural beauty. It is an enduring inspiration and truly a painter’s dr
 eam\,” says Schaffer.\n\nArt has been a focus throughout Schaffer’s li
 fe. She has been painting full time in Dry Creek since the mid-1990s and i
 s particularly known for her paintings of Sonoma County’s wine country. 
 Her work are popular with both locals and visitors who want to bring a bit
  of Sonoma’s beauty and magic into their own homes. Schaffer has been a 
 member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for more than 25 years and has exhibite
 d regionally\, including eight years as an Art Trails artist.\n\nMeet the 
 artist:  Schaffer will be hosting the Gallery on September 3 and 27 from
  11-6 pm.  \n\nStairway Showcase: Tosya Shore — “It’s Black and Wh
 ite with a Splash of Color”\n\nThe Stairway Showcase presents artist Tos
 ya Shore’s “It’s Black and White with a Splash of Color\,” a colle
 ction of watercolors that begins with the fundamentals of composition: red
 ucing an image to its two most essential elements—black and white. Worki
 ng with ink\, a stick\, and a scraper\, Shore roughens the edges of her su
 bjects and strips away unnecessary detail\, allowing light itself—not fo
 rm or precision—to take center stage. Her paintings invite the viewer to
  experience the essence of a scene through contrast\, gesture\, and the ex
 pressive qualities of the medium.\n\nIn addition to her watercolor works\,
  Shore presents paintings inspired by a recent trip to Carmel\, where she 
 picked up oil paint for the first time and explored painting the ocean usi
 ng nothing but a palette knife. The resulting works introduce a vibrant sp
 lash of color and texture into a practice grounded in restraint—new pigm
 ent\, new surface\, yet the same enduring fascination with light over like
 ness.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jeffrey Halford & The Healers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T000000
UID:260813ho8Bb18Yv0Syxozz6c5HLQ
DESCRIPTION:Of the many marks of genius associated with rock n’ roll gre
 atness\, the knack for surrounding oneself with transformational talent lo
 oms especially large\, with The Rolling Stones being perhaps the most nota
 ble example. Jeffrey Halford treads a poetic rootsy path on his latest rel
 ease\, SOUL CRUSADE\, combining a bulletproof collection of songs inspired
  by gospel\, folk\, soul\, and blues\, with a formidable roster of musical
  contributors. The result is one of Halford’s most approachable and easy
 -grooving.\n\nHis latest album release\, SOUL CRUSADE\, is the follow-up t
 o the critically acclaimed record WEST TOWARDS SOUTH. The album came out i
 n Europe on Continental Song City\, debuted in September at \\#2\, and the
 n undisputedly reached \\#1 in October 2022 and stayed in the chart for fo
 ur months. \n\nJEFFREY HALFORD & THE HEALERS are gearing up for their eigh
 th European tour in September and October 2025\, bringing their signature 
 blend of raw rock ‘n’ roll\, country\, and soul back to the stage. But
  this tour isn’t just another run—it marks the 25th anniversary of KER
 OSENE\, the album \\(release date Friday\, August 29th\, 2025\\) that put 
 Halford on the map as a true Americana troubadour.
LOCATION:The Elephant In the Room
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108309641?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
