BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T170000
UID:260903-h9wyy0yFU-9gybTITYfpw
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, **Lucci Lambrusco is taking over
  Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen**\, bringing a taste of Italian aperi
 tivo culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afterno
 on of Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made
  for lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined e
 very Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and produ
 cers\, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more 
 about what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on **Thursday\, Sep
 tember 3**\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancin
 i on the patio.\n\n**LUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER** Monday–Frid
 ay | 3:00–5:00 PM September & October\n\n**THURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES** 
 Every Thursday | 3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptem
 ber 10 | Oliver McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24
  | Idlewild Wines\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti 
 Vineyards\n\nOctober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\n**Lucci is p
 ouring all season long\, with a few friends joining along the way.**\n\nCo
 me for a glass. Stay for another.\n\n**JOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR**
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Harvest in Watercolor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260911T130000
UID:260823SJb6FqCUKUKZFTAk8IqVcQ
DESCRIPTION:Fridays Weekly · 6 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 4 – Oc
 tober 9\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory
 \n\nDrawing & Painting\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Level
 s\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$260\n\nMaterials Fee:\
 n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$290\n\nIn this six-week course\, pa
 rticipants will learn foundational watercolor techniques and develop essen
 tial experiential knowledge of this beautiful and challenging medium. Our 
 unifying subject will be gorgeous fresh produce – fruits\, veggies and h
 erbs. These subjects are great for beginners and experienced watercolor pa
 inters alike\; their organic shapes make them forgiving drawing subjects\,
  but their beauty can be a muse for life. Instructor Hannah Day is a passi
 onate produce lover and botanical painter and will share her unique approa
 ch to rendering botanicals. This class will work from life\, practicing ob
 servational drawing in addition to watercolor technique. With six class se
 ssions\, participants will have the opportunity to develop their skills an
 d build muscle memory with a medium that often feels like it has a mind of
  its own. Beginning artists and repeat students welcome! All supplies are 
 provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/fall-harvest-in-watercolor/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
