BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Reduction Linocut
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T130000
UID:260823tUPxq5oiIE64LL9uQ2mxUw
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays Weekly · 4 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 5 – 
 26\, 2026\n\n10:00 AM – 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 208\n\nCategory\n\nP
 rintmaking\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nReg
 istration Cost:\n\n$195\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cos
 t:\n\n$225\n\nIn this special four-week workshop\, participants will explo
 re the unique art of reduction relief printmaking. Acclaimed guest artist\
 , Tomoko Murakami\, will demonstrate how to create multi-color prints from
  a single linoleum block. The main idea is to gradually carve away parts o
 f the block and print each new layer of color\, with each layer building o
 n the previous one. The course covers the entire process\, from designing 
 and planning\, to carving techniques\, inking\, registration\, and printin
 g with both hand and printing press methods. Participants will learn to ex
 plore the possibilities of color mixing and layering\, enabling students t
 o achieve intricate designs and a wide range of visual effects. You will g
 ain an understanding of the materials\, processes\, and innovations involv
 ed in this unique form of relief print printing!All levels are welcome\, i
 ncluding continuing linocut students. Please note: This class requires ha
 nd dexterity to maneuver the carving tool. Participants should feel comfor
 table standing\, and using tools with sharp blades and edges.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/introduction-to-reduction-l
 inocut/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summit Saturday: Trione-Annadel SP
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T140000
UID:260822YzeqfUdA7EaNpHpmvkOZ0g
DESCRIPTION:If you have previously completed Sugarloaf's Intermediat
 e Hiking for Fitness Series\, or can hike 6.5 miles with at le
 ast 1\,600ft of elevation\, this hike may be right for you. Com
 pletion of the Bald Mountain summit hike \\(in and out via Bald
  Mountain Trail\\) is recommended as a pre-requisite. \n\nMeet at
  the main parking lot at the end of Channel Dr. The group wil
 l start out on Warren Richardson Trail\, continuing onto Two Qua
 rry Trail. At the Marsh Trail junction\, we'll trek northwest ar
 ound Buick Meadow\, connecting with South Burma Trail\, returning
  to Warren Richardson Trail and finishing through the obsidian-pe
 ppered Steve's "S" Trail. \n\nThis event requires advance registra
 tion\; day-of on site tickets will not be available. There is a
  $10 deposit per ticket\, which will be returned post-hike\, unl
 ess you choose to donate it to support this and other Sonoma E
 cology Center programs at Sugarloaf Ridge SP. Wear appropriate fo
 otwear for rocky/slippery trails\, layers\, and sun protection. Br
 ing at least 64oz of water and if desired\, a snack. Parking f
 ees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/summsat-sept2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Collage Your Story
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T150000
UID:260822GFqCAfINBU2dOwsCMCz5XQ
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 12\, 2026 11:00 am to 3:00 pm\n\nLocation
 \n\nRoom 110\n\nCategory\n\nDrawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nExperience L
 evel\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n16\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$115\n\nMater
 ials Fee:\n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$125\n\nJoin French-Americ
 an collage artist Catherine Cruz for a special\, personalized workshop des
 igned just for you! The word collage comes from the French verb coller\, m
 eaning “to glue\,” and is all about merging various materials to tell 
 a visual story. Much like our lives\, which are shaped by countless moment
 s and experiences\, collage pieces bring together fragments that reveal hi
 dden connections and untold narratives. In this class\, you’ll reflect o
 n what matters most to you and how that can be expressed through art. Cath
 erine will help you release the need for perfection and trust your creativ
 e instincts. By the end of the workshop\, you’ll not only have a finishe
 d artwork but also a deeper connection to your creative potential and a re
 newed love for the art of collage. Some of the images featured on this pag
 e show artwork created by students who have participated in Catherine’s 
 previous workshops.\n\nWhat You’ll learn\n\nCreative ways to incorporate
  your personal story in your art \n\nMethods for sourcing interesting col
 lage papers\n\nTechniques for crafting textured\, multi-layered collages\n
 \nStrategies for refining your composition\n\nRequirements\n\nPlease bring
  your own papers to personalize your artwork like ephemera that represents
  your life or a certain period of time\, copies of photos\, old letters\, 
 book pages\, papers from memorable experiences or travels\, or documents t
 hat hold meaning. If you’re not comfortable using these documents\, you 
 should make laser color copies of them. You will not be able to use anythi
 ng printed on glossy paper or photo paper so it is best to make laser copi
 es of your photographs. Inkjet prints do not work with this process.\n\nPa
 rticipants must purchase and bring the following items – Instructor will
  not provide panels for this class:\n\nOne 12”x12” cradled wood panel\
 , either ¾” thick or 1 ½” thick – panel can be purchased locally a
 t RileyStreet Art Supply or online at Blick.com – Do not use a canvas.\n
 \nApron or painting shirt\n\nNitrile gloves if you have sensitive skin\n\n
 Brown bag lunch and beverage\n\nAny collage papers you would like to use. 
 Please see website for supply list
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/collage-your-story/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
