BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2nd Annual BEE in Kenya Dinner and Art Auction
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T210000
UID:260817ZzJmC_ozmE2u78kkAFr9hQ
DESCRIPTION:*Healdsburg\, CA — \\[Sept. 12\\]* — Following the incredi
 ble success of its first sold-out and waitlisted Bee-Inspired Benefit Dinn
 er at Preston Farm and Winery and first BEE in Kenya dinner at Acorn\, Son
 oma County Bee Company is thrilled to announce their third dinner experien
 ce and **Second Annual BEE in Kenya Benefit Dinner**—an unforgettable ev
 ening celebrating community\, conservation\, and global connection.\n\nOn 
 **\\[Sept 12\\]**\, guests are invited to gather at **Dragonfly Floral** i
 n Healdsburg for a community-driven fundraising dinner benefiting **Bee in
  Kenya**\, the nonprofit co-founded by beekeeper and Sonoma County Bee Com
 pany owner **Candice Koseba**.\n\nThis year's event will also feature an *
 *all-art auction**\, with original works generously donated by an inspirin
 g collection of local and international artists. Local artists Jake Messin
 g\, Jessica Martin\, and Sebastian Pochan to name a few. Each piece has be
 en donated to help raise critical funds for BEE in Kenya's mission\, makin
 g art an integral part of an evening dedicated to creating meaningful impa
 ct.\n\n**BEE in Kenya 501(c)(3)**—short for *Beekeepers and Educators En
 gaged in Kenya*—works to empower rural Kenyan communities through ecolog
 ical education and sustainable beekeeping. The organization partners with 
 schools and community organizations throughout Kenya to foster a deeper un
 derstanding of natural ecosystems\, the essential role of bees\, and regen
 erative beekeeping practices that support environmental stewardship and lo
 ng-term economic resilience.\n\nEvery ticket purchased\, every auction bid
 \, and every donation made directly supports BEE in Kenya's programs\, hel
 ping provide beekeeping equipment\, training\, educational resources\, and
  opportunities that strengthen both communities and the landscapes they de
 pend on.\n\nAs *Sonoma Magazine* noted in its coverage of previous events:
  🔗 “An Upcoming Winery Dinner in Healdsburg Is Creating a Lot of Buzz
 ”\n\n**All proceeds from the dinner will directly support BEE in Kenya
 ’s initiatives**\, including equipment grants for rural beekeepers\, cur
 riculum development for schools\, and training workshops in sustainable ap
 iculture.\n\nTickets are limited — and if history is any indication\, th
 ey’ll sell fast. Be part of the buzz and help bring the transformative p
 ower of bees across continents.\n\n**Event Details** 📍 *Location:* Drag
 onfly Floral + Farm : 425 Westside Rd\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448 📅 *Date:*
  Saturday September 12 6-9pm 🎟 *Tickets:*2nd Annual BEE in Kenya Benefi
 t Dinner & Art Auction
LOCATION:Dragonfly Floral 
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/2nd-annual-bee-in-kenya-benefit-dinner-ar
 t-auction-tickets-1996131096845?discount=ARTISTPRICE2026&keep_tld=true
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to be OK with an Overwhelmed Mind
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T150000
UID:260817ZowpNFE6EUC_vvVf25bktQ
DESCRIPTION:with Leslie Booker\n\nLet’s first debunk the myth that our m
 ind should be completely quiet and empty of all thoughts. This is a high b
 ar to meet during our meditation practice\, and certainly not the reality 
 of a healthy mind. Just as the tongue tastes and the nose smells\, the min
 d thinks… it’s its job! The goal of meditation is not about how quiet
  and still our mind \\(and body\\) can get\, but how we respond to a mind 
 that is overwhelmed\, creative\, anxious\, dreamy\, neurodiverse\, and eve
 n a little sleepy.\n\nAnd we do this by allowing the wisdom of the body to
  take the lead.\n\nThis day is not meant to exclude\, pathologize\, or dia
 gnose anyone\, but to normalize that there is a lot happening in the mind\
 , and explore how mindfulness of the body can support us in untangling and
  regulating the nervous system to reduce some of that anxiety.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/how-to-be-ok-with-an-o
 verwhelmed-mind-coming-home-to-the-wisdom-of-the-body-lb1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ARTIST RECEPTION FEATURING BOBBIE BURGERS: DEPTH OF FIELD
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T180000
UID:260817TvoizCV1sU2edV7nQJnpDg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 12\, 2026 | 4:00–6:00 PM Caldwell Snyde
 r Gallery | 1328 Main Street\, St. Helena\, CA\n\nCaldwell Snyder Gallery 
 is pleased to present Depth of Field\, a solo exhibition of new works by a
 cclaimed Canadian artist Bobbie Burgers. Join us on Saturday\, September 1
 2\, from 4–6 PM for a Conversation with the Artist & Book Signing celebr
 ating the exhibition.\n\nFor more than two decades\, Burgers has developed
  a distinctive contemporary painting practice defined by vibrant color\, e
 xpressive gesture\, and richly layered surfaces. Blurring the line between
  abstraction and representation\, her paintings transform florals and orga
 nic forms into immersive compositions inspired by the rhythms\, growth\, a
 nd fleeting beauty of the natural world.\n\nBorn in Vancouver\, British Co
 lumbia\, Burgers has exhibited extensively throughout Canada\, the United 
 States\, Europe\, and China. Caldwell Snyder Gallery has proudly represent
 ed the artist since 2002.\n\nDepth of Field will be on view through Septem
 ber 30\, 2026.\n\nEvent Details: Saturday\, September 12\, 2026 4:00–6:0
 0 PM Caldwell Snyder Gallery 1328 Main Street St. Helena\, CA 94574\n\nFre
 e and open to the public.
LOCATION:Caldwell Snyder Gallery
URL:https://www.caldwellsnyder.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
