BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T170000
UID:260803uFOce_4Hzk6rQPPZFf19Mw
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Equivocation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T193000
UID:260803snDQHM6Qn0GmpQQ4hHqAQg
DESCRIPTION:England\, 1605: A terrorist plot is brewing to assassinate Kin
 g James 1 and blow Parliament to kingdom come! Or so the King claims. To s
 pread his propaganda\, King James 1 hires the world’s most famous playwr
 ight\, William Shagspeare (after a contemporary spelling of the Bard’s n
 ame). As Shag investigates the King’s bizarre tale\, he begins to questi
 on it\, leading him and his actors to a dilemma: lie and pocket the cash\,
  tell the truth and literally risk their necks\, or perhaps equivocate–l
 ie and tell the truth at the same time. This high-stakes thriller drops in
 to many of the Bard’s most famous works in an alternate history that res
 onates today. This is a witty and poignant ensemble piece in which six act
 ors play well over a dozen roles\, some of which include snippets of Shake
 speare's other plays-in-progress (one of which becomes the famous Macbeth.
 )
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/equivocation/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jack London State Historic Park WILD Trail Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T090000
UID:260803ppCJ3NPjA0asQMa9Npjs3Q
DESCRIPTION:On Saturdays from Sept. 5 to Oct. 3\, Jack London State Histor
 ic Park’s WILD Trail Challenge returns for a third year.  This series o
 f five hikes covers every trail in the park for a total of 39.5 miles.  T
 he hikes increase in duration and/or difficulty each week.\n\nParticipants
  can sign up for individual hikes or do them all.\n\nThe price for each hi
 ke is $15.  The park entry fee of $15 per vehicle is waived for these hik
 es.  Those who sign up for all five hikes before Sept. 5 save 20 percent 
 and pay only $60.\n\nHike # 1 – Historic Trails\n\nSeptember 5\, 9 a.m.-
 12:30 p.m.  \n\nA great way to warm up. This hike explores the historic s
 ites and trails of the park. Navigate both sides of the park to discover J
 ack London’s Beauty Ranch\, London Lake\, and the Wolf House ruins.\n\nE
 asy – moderate hike (approximately 4.5 miles roundtrip)\n\nHike # 2 – 
 Ancient Redwood\n\nSeptember 12\, 9 a.m.-1 p.m.   \n\nMeander through th
 e redwoods and sunny oak woodlands of the park’s three Bridge Trails (Up
 per\, Lower\, and Fallen). The journey leads to the majestic ancient redwo
 od\, fondly known as the Grandmother Tree.\n\nModerate hike (approximately
  6 miles roundtrip)\n\nHike # 3 – Historic Orchard\n\nSeptember 19\, 9 a
 .m.-1:30 p.m.   \n\nStart Location: Note that this hike does not begin a
 t Jack London State Historic Park\n\nSonoma Developmental Center\n\nArnold
  Dr\, Eldridge\, CA 95431\n\nStroll along the blue shores of Fern Lake bef
 ore reaching the Historic Orchard. Learn about the history of the land and
  the fascinating fruit-bearing crops that thrive there.\n\nModerate – Di
 fficult hike (approximately 7 miles roundtrip)\n\nHike # 4 – Ridge\n\nSe
 ptember 26\, 9 a.m-3:30 p.m.   \n\nDetails: Hikers will gain elevation a
 nd an appreciation for the diverse habitats found within the park. They’
 ll also traverse part of the ever-growing Bay Area Ridge Trail.\n\nDifficu
 lt hike (approximately 12 miles roundtrip)\n\nHike # 5 – Summit \n\nOct
 ober 3\, 9 a.m.-2:30 p.m.     \n\nA trek to the park summit is the per
 fect way to complete the WILD Trail Challenges.  Climb Sonoma Mountain to
  enjoy stunning views\, celebrate with fellow hikers\, and become a WILD O
 ne.\n\nDifficult hike (approximately 10 miles roundtrip)
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/wild-trail-challenge-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
