SUMMARY:Guided Nature Walk & Ranch House tour Anderson Marsh
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260912T110000
UID:260826DMlE1YTRlEeO_Ydj89tiYQ
DESCRIPTION:The next “Second Saturday” Guided Nature walk at Anderson 
 Marsh State Historic Park will be held on Saturday\, September 12\, 2026. 
 \n\nThe Guided Walk will begin at 8:30am. Bring binoculars and meet in the
  parking lot at 8:15am for an opportunity to observe the birds and other w
 ildlife found in the picnic area. Sturdy shoes\, a hat and water are sugge
 sted. \n\nThe September guided walk will be led by State Parks volunteer d
 ocent Roberta Lyons and will provide an opportunity to observe wildlife at
  the park and learn about their natural habitat\, as well as to learn abou
 t the natural and cultural history of the area. \n\nThe walk will take bet
 ween 1½ and 2 hours\, depending on the route taken. Dogs are not allowed 
 on the park trails. \n\nA tour of the historic Anderson Ranch House will b
 e available immediately after the conclusion of the walk. \n\nThere is no 
 charge for the Nature Walk and Ranch House tour and parking is free for th
 ose attending.
LOCATION:Anderson Marsh State Historic Park
URL:https://lakecounty.com/event/guided-nature-walk-ranch-house-tour-ander
 son-marsh/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
