SUMMARY:Séptima Dia Anual de Kelseyville de la Independencia 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T200000
UID:260625sJBbgfGXEkWml2qEzSbouQ
DESCRIPTION:Disfrute de la 7.ª celebración anual del Día de la Independ
 encia en Kelseyville\, un festival tradicional mexicano que tendrá lugar 
 en Main Street. El evento contará con una presentación de Los Amigos Dan
 cing Horses y música en vivo para ambientar esta gran celebración\, ¡co
 n la participación de la Banda La Conquistadora de San José\, California
 ! Paquiyollotzin\, el Ballet Folclórico de Petaluma\, también se present
 ará para celebrar la preservación de la rica cultura de México a travé
 s del canto y la danza. ¡Excelente música\, deliciosa comida y actividad
 es para los niños\, que incluyen castillos inflables\, pintura facial y p
 iñatas! ¡Venga ataviado con vestimenta o traje tradicional mexicano y po
 dría ganar un fantástico premio! ¡Entrada gratuita para el público! \\
 *\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\
 \*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*
 \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* Enjoy Kelseyville's 7th annual Dia de la Independ
 encia\, a traditional Mexican festival on Main Street\, Kelseyville featur
 ing a performance from Los Amigos Dancing Horses and live music to set the
  scene for this great celebration\, with  Banda La Conquistadora de san jo
 se california! Paquiyollotzin\, Ballet Folklorico of Petaluma will also be
  performing to celebrate preserving Mexico’s rich culture through song a
 nd dance.  Great music\, great food\, and kids' activities including jump 
 houses\, face painting\, and piñatas! Come in traditional Mexican attire/
 costume and you could win a great prize! Free to the public! Vendors:  htt
 ps://forms.gle/fbCfAijt9bWcWEAo7
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1282921197216608/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sturgeon’s Mill Open Demonstration Run
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T150000
UID:260610g5DN8ru9dUCzgYf8bwVXOQ
DESCRIPTION:Step into a true piece of California history at Sturgeon’s M
 ill\, a fully operational **steam-powered sawmill founded in 1914**. Unlik
 e a replica\, this is an authentic working museum where the **original mac
 hinery still runs today**\, offering a rare chance to see early 20th-centu
 ry industry in action.\n\n**Dates:** June 20-21 | August 1-2 | September 1
 2-13\n\n**Time:** 10:00 AM - 3:00 PM (crew breaks for lunch 12:00 PM -1:00
  PM)\n\n**Location:** 2150 Green Hill Rd\, Sebastopol\, CA\n\nWatch live s
 team demonstrations as the mill comes to life\, explore historic equipment
 \, and learn how local lumber mills helped build Sonoma County and the gre
 ater Bay Area. Docent-led tours run throughout the day\, or you can explor
 e at your own pace.\n\nCome experience the sights\, sounds\, and stories o
 f a working mill where history still runs on steam.\n\n**Highlights:**\n\n
 Live operation of a historic steam-powered sawmill\n\nAll-original equipme
 nt from over 100 years ago\n\nGuided tours and hands-on exploration\n\nBla
 cksmith shop\, gardens\, and farm animals\n\nFood available for purchase f
 rom the cook shack\n\nBring a picnic and enjoy the beautiful redwood setti
 ng\n\n**Good to Know:**\n\nAdmission is **free - no tickets required**\n\n
 Donations are appreciated to support preservation\n\nFree parking availabl
 e on site.
LOCATION:Sturgeon's Mill
URL:http://www.sturgeonsmill.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
