BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Red
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T130000
UID:260715RfLQmjDfh0uTGzaT7U4Q_Q
DESCRIPTION:Red is a critically acclaimed 2010 Tony Award-winning play by 
 John Logan that explores the intense\, tumultuous relationship between abs
 tract expressionist painter Mark Rothko and his fictional assistant\, Ken\
 , in the late 1950s. The two-person drama delves into themes of art\, ambi
 tion\, mentorship\, and the generational shift from Abstract Expressionism
  to Pop Art\, set against the backdrop of Rothko's high-stakes Seagram mur
 als commission. The theatre programming of Red will be complimented by two
  additional events:  The Art in Red on Monday\, September 14 at 6 pm.  Red
 \, Rothko\, and You on Monday\, September 21 at 5 pm
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/red/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Workshop: Pasta Machine Printing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260913T160000
UID:2607136SEm13Fxn0i1xVyfdDzmhw
DESCRIPTION:Revive your manual pasta maker by learning how to use it to cr
 eate small drypoint prints. This technique uses the pressure that normally
  rolls out the pasta dough to printartwork. Students will learn how to use
  different materials to create a plate including milk cartons\, Tetra Paks
 \, and Akua plate material. They'll learn how to ink up the plate\, add pa
 cking to the pasta maker for the perfect impression\, and pull prints to m
 ake a small edition. The small-format prints created in class will be up t
 o 4" by 6". Prints will be made using a drypoint needle and a cutting knif
 e and will be printed on different kinds of print making paper. \\*The pas
 ta machine does not get any ink on it\, so using it for pasta AND printing
  is perfectly fine. Oil based etching ink will be used during class\; the 
 instructor will demonstrate how easy it is to clean up without any heavy c
 leaning solution. Available Dates Sunday\, September 13th 10:00am - 4:00pm
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/workshop-pasta-machine-printing/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
