BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Visiting Artist Lecture Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T125000
UID:260902LGnWrtMM2UilFcnExGlXQA
DESCRIPTION:September 17 - Andrew Owen is a photographer working primarily
  in the tradition of large-format landscape photography. Since 2021\, he h
 as followed the cycles of fires and floods reshaping the California landsc
 ape\, documenting major ecological events and their aftermath to understan
 d the impact of climate change. Andrew's work has been published online in
  the New York Times and exhibited in San Francisco at Small Works Projects
  and group shows at CULT Aimee Friberg and Book and Job Gallery. He is a f
 ormer National Geographic Young Explorer grantee and graduate of Georgetow
 n University.
LOCATION:Sonoma State University
URL:https://art.sonoma.edu/visiting-artist-lecture-series
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Conversation: In-Between Spaces\, The Art of Garden Transit
 ions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260917T200000
UID:2609029WIQQ0EgwEKOZJ4l4ylzng
DESCRIPTION:Featuring more than 90 photographs of gardens and landscapes\,
  explore local author Louise Leff's book as it looks closely at the moment
 s that connect one space to another and the many ways those transitions in
 fluence how we see and experience a garden.\n\n"The spaces between one gar
 den area and another are often overlooked\, yet they can be some of the mo
 st memorable parts of a landscape."\n\nPrepare to explore this beautiful b
 ook\, discuss with landscaping expert Louise Leff\, and enjoy some light r
 efreshments with us.\n\n\\- Louise Leff
LOCATION:Usher Gallery
