BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boz Scaggs Rhythm Review 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260918T193000
UID:2609048cAnSNiN0UyZKUKAIgLTKA
DESCRIPTION:Boz Scaggs Friday\, September 18 at 7:30 p.m. Tickets $45–$1
 25 Weill Hall \\+ Lawn Boz Scaggs is an American singer\, songwriter\, and
  guitarist. An early bandmate of Steve Miller in The Ardells and the Steve
  Miller Band\, he began his solo career in 1969\, though he lacked a major
  hit until his 1976 album Silk Degrees peaked at number 2 on the Billboard
  200\, and produced the hit singles “Lido Shuffle” and “Lowdown”. 
 Scaggs produced two more platinum- certified albums in Down Two Then Left 
 and Middle Man\, the latter of which produced two top-40 singles “Breakd
 own Dead Ahead” and “Jojo”. After a hiatus for most of the 1980s\, h
 e returned to recording and touring in 1988\, joining The New York Rock an
 d Soul Revue and opening the nightclub Slim’s\, a popular San Francisco 
 music venue until it closed in 2020. He has continued to record and tour t
 hroughout the 1990s\, 2000s\, and 2010s\, with his album being 2018’s Ou
 t of the Blues. Info and tickets at https://gmc.sonoma.edu/boz-scaggs
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/848749100898103/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
