DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, September 20\, 2026\n\nSession 1: 10:00 AM – 1:00
  PM Session 2: 2:00 PM – 5:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 110\n\nCategory\n\n
 Events\, Fiber Arts\, Other\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\nA
 ll Ages\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$10\n\nIn this playful half-day wor
 kshop\, participants will create whimsical illuminated lanterns using vell
 um\, paper\, tissue\, color\, and light. Inspired by nature\, memory\, ima
 gination\, and celebratio Together we will explore basic lantern-building 
 techniques while creating meaningful objects to honor ancestors\, loved on
 es\, and the cycles of life.  Participants are invited to add wishes\, bl
 essings\, names\, drawings\, or messages of remembrance to their lanterns.
  This workshop is designed to be welcoming\, creative\, and accessible for
  beginners and mixed ages. Children are welcome with adult participation. 
 Come create a lantern to carry into the autumn—a  beacon of memory\, be
 auty\, and community light!\n\nRequired Supply List\n\nPlease bring the fo
 llowing supplies to the class:\n\nPruning Shears\n\nSketchbook\n\nOptional
 : Meaningful images\, poems\, or small materials to inspire your design
