UID:260822BOa3LpiEnEeUxoXkyLoVHQ
DESCRIPTION:**BRING OUT YOUR SPARKLING CLASSICS\, YOUR JOYFUL JALOPIES & Y
 OUR BELOVED BEATERS (or just yourselves!) & JOIN THE FUN.**\n\n**Long Snak
 e Monte Rio** is proud to present our 3rd Annual matinee + day of communit
 y fun on Sunday\, September 20th\, 2026 at the iconic **Monte Rio Theater 
 & Extravaganza**\, in Monte Rio\, California.  Car Show at 12:30pm.  Awa
 rds & Film Screening at 2pm. \n\n Special guests from the **Redwood Empi
 re Chevy Club**\, **Corvettes of Sonoma County & Redwood Empire Region of 
 the Antique Automobile** **Club** will grace the lawn of the iconic 7-year
 -old Quonset Hut-turned movie theater in a dazzling spectacle of automotiv
 e design.  The community is welcomed to arrive an hour and a half before 
 screening time to ogle the classic cars and cast a vote for their favorite
  car (in exchange for Kitty Joe’s key lime pie).  Prizes for the top 3 
 favorite cars have been generously donated by Wonderland Pizzeria (Monte R
 io)\, The Siren’s Cellar (Jenner) & Cochineal (Freestone)\n\n**Chef Dave
  Mau** will be serving up his ever-popular Tri-Tip Sandwiches (vegetarian 
 alt available)\, for lunch.\n\n**\\*\\*If you would like to enter your cla
 ssic in the car show\, please email longsnakemonterio@gmail.com**
LOCATION:Monte Rio Theater & Extravaganza
URL:https://www.monteriotheater.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slow Reptile Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T130000
UID:260821EHw2WGfzhUKDZa96J2jVsg
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbirds\, the taste of a Douglas Fir
  needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or w
 atching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and ins
 ects in the grass?  Each month \\(weather permitting\\) we will
  explore one or two of our accessible trails-- the Creekside  
 Nature Trail\, and the Meadow Trail. Suitable for all levels and
  a range of mobility\, these Sunday afternoon adventures will ac
 commodate people using walkers or wheelchairs\, young children\, p
 arents with babies in strollers\, as well as those who just enj
 oy slow walks in nature that stimulate the five senses. \n\nOur
  September outing will focus on the reptiles of Sugarloaf. Ticke
 ts are $5 for adults and free for children under 18 years of 
 age. All minors must be accompanied by parent or legal guardian.
  Tickets day-of\, on site will be $10 and might not be availab
 le. Meet at the day use picnic area\, across from the main par
 king lot.\n\nThere will be frequent stops and opportunities for c
 onversation\, photography\, nature journaling\, wildlife viewing\, r
 esting\, etc.\, so bring your nature journal\, camera\, or binocu
 lars if you have them. Wear comfortable shoes\, a hat\, sun pro
 tection\, bring water and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees app
 ly.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/26-sepjourn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:macbitches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T153000
UID:260820s-R5lOX2hEe4WjCaTjNLHQ
DESCRIPTION:“macbitches takes Shakespearean themes and grounds them in 
 a recognizable\, modern reality — a smarter\, theater-centered Mean Gir
 ls\, if you will. It’s funny\, sharp\, and unafraid to let women be comp
 licated.” - Jeanette Seisdedos\, director\n\nmacbitches takes a darkly 
 funny look at the toxic\, high-stakes world of university theater\, center
 ing on a freshman who unexpectedly lands the role of Lady Macbeth. The pla
 y centers on freshman acting major Hailey\, who unexpectedly scores the co
 veted role of Lady Macbeth. Her upperclassmen rivals immediately invite he
 r over to “celebrate.” As the Fireball and Svedka flow\, the young wom
 en interrogate their own ambitions as well as the power structures that ha
 ve shaped their education—and when the night spirals into violent and sh
 ocking acts of betrayal\, they come to learn that what’s done cannot be 
 undone.\n\n\\*Content Advisory: Strong profanity\, physical and psycholog
