BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Pacific
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T170000
UID:260803H0MOCcPERUqhLn3em_MhXA
DESCRIPTION:**An unforgettable romance set against the sweeping tides of W
 orld War II.**\n\nAgainst the backdrop of the Pacific War of WWII\, ***Sou
 th Pacific*** blends high-stakes wartime romance with a poignant explorati
 on of social prejudice. When spirited Navy nurse\, Nellie Forbush\, falls 
 in love with a sophisticated French planter\, and a young Marine lieutenan
 t finds himself captivated by an ethereal island girl\, their relationship
 s are tested by the prejudices and pressures of a world at war. What unfol
 ds is a deeply moving story about love\, courage\, and the transformative 
 power of understanding. Featuring a soaring score by **Richard Rodgers** a
 nd **Oscar Hammerstein II**\, including classics like “Some Enchanted Ev
 ening” and “There Is Nothin’ Like a Dame\,” *South Pacific* remain
 s one of the most beloved musicals of all time.\n\nWinner of the 1950 Puli
 tzer Prize for Drama\, the original Broadway production won ten Tony Award
 s\, including Best Musical\, Best Score and Best Libretto. It is the only 
 musical production ever to have won all four Tony Awards for acting.\n\nSO
 UTH PACIFIC is presented by arrangement with Concord Theatricals on behalf
  of The Rodgers & Hammerstein Organization. concordtheatricals.com\n\nPerf
 ormances run Thur\, Friday\, Saturday evenings at 7:30pm and Saturday and 
 Sunday matinees at 2:00pm.
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/rodgers-hammersteins-south-pacifi
 c/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ravi Coltrave Quartet: Centennial Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T210000
UID:2607213dqF8Jg81kGmkmUP6IGfWQ
DESCRIPTION:Just days before John Coltrane would have turned 100\, his son
 \, saxophonist Ravi Coltrane\, presents a blazing young band to mark the m
 ilestone. Ravi\, 60\, spent the first quarter-century of his career acquir
 ing a diverse array of experience and honing his own lustrous\, harmonical
 ly slippery compositions. But in recent years he’s taken up the family m
 antle with a variety of projects and initiatives on and off the bandstand\
 , championing the legacy of both his parents\, John and Alice Coltrane. \
 n\nFor this celebration\, he’s joined by the brilliant trumpeter Jonatha
 n Finlayson\, a longtime collaborator who graduated from Berkeley High. Is
 raeli pianist/keyboardist Gadi Lehavi made his Village Vanguard debut with
  Ravi at 15. Now 30\, he’s more than lived up to his enormous potential.
  Powering the quartet is Bay Area-reared drum sensation Elé Howell\, 28\,
  a supremely musical accompanist who gained national attention when Coltra
 ne started hiring him in 2021 for various projects\, including Cosmic Musi
 c: Revisiting the Music of John and Alice Coltrane.\n\nJohn Coltrane's pre
 sence continues to illuminate new directions for exploration. Join us for 
 this special Centennial Celebration with Ravi Coltrane and his band.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://healdsburgjazz.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
