DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T130000
UID:260715wlF0KPTxSUSUHraWqxLxZQ
DESCRIPTION:Red is a critically acclaimed 2010 Tony Award-winning play by 
 John Logan that explores the intense\, tumultuous relationship between abs
 tract expressionist painter Mark Rothko and his fictional assistant\, Ken\
 , in the late 1950s. The two-person drama delves into themes of art\, ambi
 tion\, mentorship\, and the generational shift from Abstract Expressionism
  to Pop Art\, set against the backdrop of Rothko's high-stakes Seagram mur
 als commission. The theatre programming of Red will be complimented by two
  additional events:  The Art in Red on Monday\, September 14 at 6 pm.  Red
 \, Rothko\, and You on Monday\, September 21 at 5 pm
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/red/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
