BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between Two Plantsmen: Sean Hogan in Conversation with Jim Salyard
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
UID:260904OgpAmJ3YrEStd1gZElAY1A
DESCRIPTION:What can a lifetime with plants teach us?\n\nJoin Sean Hogan\,
  founder of Cistus Nursery and Gardens\, and Jim Salyards\, Associate Dire
 ctor of Garden Experience at Filoli\, for an intimate conversation at West
 ern Hills Garden.\n\nLong-time friends and fellow plantsmen\, Sean and Jim
  will reflect on horticulture\, legacy gardens\, plant exploration\, and t
 he enduring relationships between people and place.\n\nExpect an evening o
 f stories\, insights\, and thoughtful conversation for gardeners\, horticu
 lturalists\, and anyone who loves the natural world.\n\nThis talk is part 
 of *Western Hills Garden’s Horticultural Exchange Series*\, bringing tog
 ether leading voices in horticulture for thoughtful public conversations.\
 n\nSpeaker Bios:\n\nSean Hogan: Sean is an acclaimed horticulturist\, gard
 en consultant\, speaker\, and international plant collector. Convinced to 
 become California’s first certified arborist by Western Hills Garden fou
 nder Marshall Olbrich\, Sean has had a storied career as a Curator at the 
 University of California Botanical Garden at Berkeley\, and in 1996 he and
  his partner Parker founded Cistus Design Nursery on Sauvie Island in Oreg
 on. Sean is a Founding Board Member of the new Portland Botanical Garden a
 nd a member of the WHG Horticultural Advisory Committee.\n\nJim Salyards: 
 Jim has worked at Filoli for 30 years\, moving into his current role as As
 sociate Director of Garden Experience in early 2025. Jim oversees a wide r
 ange of programs that support Filoli’s external relations\, learning and
  engagement\, development\, retail\, and interpretive strategies\, with a 
 particular emphasis on community engagement. He also oversees Filoli’s p
 lant collections work and is responsible for building and nurturing relati
 onships within the fields of public gardens\, horticultural science\, gard
 ening\, retail product production\, and the culinary arts.
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/in-conversation-sept2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T171500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T200000
UID:260902Kh_v0x3_t0-tLEfM4RLrQA
DESCRIPTION:Bring a flashlight and your sense of wonder as you e
 xplore the park after dark. This moderate-to-strenuous\, 4.2-mile 
 hike with approximately 800ft of elevation gain heads up to the
  viewpoint on Vista Trail where we will see the moon rise over
  the Mayacamas and the sun set over Sonoma Valley. Not recommen
 ded for children under 7 years old.\n\nMeet at the White Barn p
 arking lot at least 10 minutes prior to 6:00 pm for a prompt 
 departure. Tickets are $10 for general audiences\, $5 for student
 s\, youth \\(12-17 year olds\\)\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf or
  RFO volunteers\, and free for children 7-11 years old. All min
 ors must be accompanied by a parent or legal guardian. You must
  register on this page to attend\; tickets on site will not be
  available. Bring your flashlight\, at least a quart of water\,
  extra layers for the evening\, and if desired\, a snack. Parki
 ng fees apply
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/sep2026moon-vista
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
