BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Habitaat & Yemanjo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T000000
UID:260813qlz6JQ_QPEChPLY1HrKU4A
DESCRIPTION:HABITAAT \\(Tomas Wischerath\\) is a San Francisco based DJ\, 
 composer\, and producer who is pushing the boundaries between organic bass
  and high-energy dance music\, creating a sound he describes as “electro
 nic music inspired by nature”. Born in Brazil and raised in the Bay Area
 \, HABITAAT’s sound is deeply influenced by hip-hop beats\, cinematic mo
 vie scores\, and underground dance music—crafting immersive sonic landsc
 apes that transport listeners to a world where rhythm meets the raw beauty
  of the earth. Blending infectious dance beats and ethereal melodic sounds
 \, HABITAAT’s soundscapes mirror the beauty of our own natural world in 
 danceable and psychedelic ways. \n\nA rising force in indie electronic mus
 ic\, HABITAAT has graced legendary stages\, including opening for CloZee a
 t Red Rocks in 2022\, and sharing lineups with artists like Bonobo and Duk
 e Dumont. HABITAAT has become a staple in both ecstatic dance and electron
 ic festival circuits. With a growing catalog of music\, including two albu
 m releases in 2024 \\(Grow\, Fall In Deep\\)\, his work continues to explo
 re what connects us to nature through sound. \n\nHABITAAT’s music resona
 tes with both deep-listening organic bass DJs and feel-good partygoers\, o
 ffering an experience that is as meditative as it is high-energy. Whether 
 played in the depths of a forest\, the pulse of a nightclub\, or under the
  stars at a festival\, HABITAAT’s music creates a space where movement\,
  connection\, and nature unite.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039507235?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laura Benitez and the Heartache
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T000000
UID:260813iWnx_0aGvEGjzyNHY97AEg
DESCRIPTION:Laura Benitez and the Heartache use the three chord tools of c
 ountry music to tell the simple\, unvarnished truth about love\, too much 
 whiskey\, and the call of the road. Their new album\, "California Centurie
 s\," finds the band delving deep into themes of collective denial \\("Bad 
 Things"\\)\, gaslighting \\("Invisible" and "Gaslight"\\) and romantic les
 sons learned \\("I'm the One" and "Are You Using Your Heart"\\). Their twa
 ngy honesty shines through in straightforward arrangements\, crystalline h
 armonies\, and spare instrumentation. Beware their catchy hooks and sweet 
 melodies - these stray puppy tunes will follow you home and become your mo
 st steadfast companions.
LOCATION:Rio Nido Roadhouse
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108578688?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T180000
UID:260813VtV9tr6V-Emhp4b7xZ-csQ
DESCRIPTION:EPTEMBER ART EXHIBIT:  THE DAYS OF VINES AND ROSES\n\nDate: 
 FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  8/12/26\n\nDATES: August 31 – September 27\, 20
 26\n\nRECEPTION:  SATURDAY\, September 5 – 3 -6 pm Join Donna Schaff
 er and Tosya Shore to celebrate the show and learn about their artistic i
 nspirations.  Refreshments will be served.  \n\nFeatured Artist Donna 
 Schaffer Celebrates Wine Country Beauty in “The Days of Vines and Roses
 ”\n\nSonoma County artist Donna Schaffer unveils her latest collection o
 f oil paintings\, “The Days of Vines and Roses\,” celebrating some of 
 her favorite views of roses blooming among the vineyards\, hills\, and woo
 dlands of Sonoma County. At the heart of the collection is Vines and Trell
 is of Roses\, where glorious pink roses spill across an entrance trellis\,
  set against the orderly rows of a vineyard. In Mini Red Roses Along Viney
 ard\, delicate red roses punctuate the landscape\, creating a lively inter
 play between vineyard rows\, stands of trees\, and the hills beyond. “Li
 ving here in Sonoma County for three decades\, I never tire of its gloriou
 s natural beauty. It is an enduring inspiration and truly a painter’s dr
 eam\,” says Schaffer.\n\nArt has been a focus throughout Schaffer’s li
 fe. She has been painting full time in Dry Creek since the mid-1990s and i
 s particularly known for her paintings of Sonoma County’s wine country. 
 Her work are popular with both locals and visitors who want to bring a bit
  of Sonoma’s beauty and magic into their own homes. Schaffer has been a 
 member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for more than 25 years and has exhibite
 d regionally\, including eight years as an Art Trails artist.\n\nMeet the 
 artist:  Schaffer will be hosting the Gallery on September 3 and 27 from
  11-6 pm.  \n\nStairway Showcase: Tosya Shore — “It’s Black and Wh
 ite with a Splash of Color”\n\nThe Stairway Showcase presents artist Tos
 ya Shore’s “It’s Black and White with a Splash of Color\,” a colle
 ction of watercolors that begins with the fundamentals of composition: red
 ucing an image to its two most essential elements—black and white. Worki
 ng with ink\, a stick\, and a scraper\, Shore roughens the edges of her su
 bjects and strips away unnecessary detail\, allowing light itself—not fo
 rm or precision—to take center stage. Her paintings invite the viewer to
  experience the essence of a scene through contrast\, gesture\, and the ex
 pressive qualities of the medium.\n\nIn addition to her watercolor works\,
  Shore presents paintings inspired by a recent trip to Carmel\, where she 
 picked up oil paint for the first time and explored painting the ocean usi
 ng nothing but a palette knife. The resulting works introduce a vibrant sp
 lash of color and texture into a practice grounded in restraint—new pigm
 ent\, new surface\, yet the same enduring fascination with light over like
 ness.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grizfolk & The Lone Bellow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T000000
UID:2608133890mx8QBkOS2d8OdtuvnQ
DESCRIPTION:Grizfolk burst onto the scene with their 2014 debut EP\, From 
 the Spark\, followed by 2016’s full-length Waking Up The Giants\, from w
 heir catchy blend of electronic-tinged folk-rock and pop styles caught the
  ears of fans around the globe. They returned in 2019 with Rarest Of Birds
 \, delivering a nostalgic\, summertime feel with their embracing more orga
 nic instrumentation in lieu of previous synth-heavy sounds.  In 2021 they 
 shared their 3rd full-length album\, the self-titled Grizfolk. It succeeds
  as a mix of both worlds that their previous albums created\, while also a
 chieving the sound the band has been chasing all along\, which Billboard c
 alled “a little country\, a little rock and a lot catchy\,” Half of th
 e new songs were produced by Rich Costey \\(Muse\, The Killers\, Barns Cou
 rtney\\) in early 2020 after the band returned from an inspiring retreat i
 n Joshua Tree. These include long-time fan favorite “The Ripple\,” whi
 ch has been a staple of their live set thanks to its Americana twang and i
 rresistible singalong appeal but had never been captured in the studio\, a
 long with the harmonica-led “Money\,” the relentless hip-shaker and he
 ad-nodder “Queen of the Desert\,” and the sunny\, confident “Califor
 nia High.” The new album is available now and tour tickets are on sale n
 ow!
LOCATION:Little Saint
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108670882?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
