BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DAVID NELSON BAND RIDES AGAIN Campout 5
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
UID:260430ABwVzxFqLUKhm3iwLhnD9w
DESCRIPTION: \n\nSeptember 26 &amp\; 27\, 20261 &amp\; 2 Day Camping Event
 \n\nHermitage Music presents:\n\nDAVID NELSON BAND RIDES AGAIN Campout 5\n
 \n                                                                        
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                                                           
                                        \n\n\n\n \n\nWelcome to the 5th Ann
 ual David Nelson Band Rides Again Weekend. Make sure to get your tickets p
 urchased early\, as tickets are going fast. We will be sending traveling d
 irections to all Ticket Holders. Please purchase tickets before the event 
 and preferably not at the door.\n\nA joyous Summer gathering of music! Thi
 s uplifting experience leaves everyone feeling grateful for being in atten
 dance. Lots of space to roam freely with friends. Views in all directions.
  Hiking trails\, Swimming for the kids at the Pool with adults present. Ki
 ds are free 12 yrs. and under. Arts &amp\; Crafts for kids. Lots of Craft 
 Vendors. \n\nService Dogs are accepted as long as they are accredited. In 
 the past dogs were free to come\, but owners let them roam freely. No camp
 fires or cooking. \n\nThere will be Food provided for Breakfast\, Lunch &a
 mp\; Dinner\, &amp\; Breakfast Latte Bar choices in the tasting room\, all
  for purchase. Free Spring Water. \\(please bring your water bottles\\).  
 Beverages\, Beer\, Wine\, &amp\; Soft Drinks all for purchase in the Tasti
 ng Room\,  2 Free Wine Tasting tickets per day.\n\nAll are welcome: friend
 s\, family &amp\; kids\, to spend 1 or 2 amazing days of camping or come f
 or the day\, Sat. or Sun.  RVs come set up early on Fri 9/25 at 3:00 to 7p
 m. Gates open on Sat. &amp\; Sun. 9/26 &amp\; 9/27 at 10:00 am. Load out y
 our campsite by noon on Monday. \n\nCAMPING AT THE EVENT Bring shade items
 \, sunscreen\, misquito spray. We will have misters and shade\, plus you c
 an chill in the Star Stage Barnand tasting room and still see the main sta
 ge. Best to stay out of the direct sun for long periods of time. \n\nBring
 : flashlights &amp\; camping gear\, hiking boots\, swimsuits &amp\; beach 
 towels\, low back chairs\, We have warm summer nights with cool breezes fr
 om the coast in the afternoon\,bring warm clothes for night time temps\, j
 ust in case it gets cold this time of year.\n\n We have 2 Hot Water Star S
 howers and dressing rooms. The Indoor Star Stage in the main indoor center
  of the barn &amp\; green room for Musicians to chill.There will be bands 
 playing in between acts on the The Corral Stage &amp\; The Star Stage\, wh
 ile the Main Galaxy Stage is getting geared up for the next bands. See the
  Line up posted around. Our wine &amp\; olive oil are for purchase &amp\; 
 visit our merch table in the tasting room. \n\nThere is Camping available 
 for all. The Fox Grove: Tent &amp\; Auto Camping\, The Oak Grove: RV Parki
 ng only. Please bring RVs in Friday from 3 -7pm. Electric hook up fee is i
 ncluded in ticket price. Bucks Corral: Tent camping only no vehicles aloud
 \, plus VIP Tent Camping. Eagle Camp:Extreme wilderness camping with 4WD o
 nly. Hikers can hike to Eagles Camp for more awesome views!\n\nTo become a
  Volunteer or to be a Merch Vendor contact hermitagemusicmgmt@proton.me\n\
 nHOTELS BOOK FAST \n\nIf you prefer not to camp\, there are other accommod
 ations available in Cloverdale\, Geyserville\, Healdsburg\, Hopland\, Boon
 ville &amp\; Ukiah.\n\nTICKETS must be purchased before these EVENTS and t
 hen you will receive directions to the Events through an email from CalTix
 .com before the Event. Cloverdale is 15 mins. from the event.\n\nCLOVERDAL
 E: SUPER 8: Call 707- 893-7057 - Furber Ranch Plaza. Address: 1147 S Clove
 rdale Blvd\, Cloverdale\, CA 95425. Only 15 minutes from venue.\n\nCLOVERD
 ALE WINE COUNTRY INN &amp\; SUITES: Call 707-894-7500 Address: 324 S Clove
 rdale Blvd\, Cloverdale\, CA 95425. Only 15 minutes from venue.\n\nGEYSERV
 ILLE INN: Call 707- 857-4343 Address: 21714 Geyserville Ave\, Geyserville\
 , CA 95441 Only 20 minutes from venue. \n\nGEYSERVILLE: ISIS OASIS: Call 7
 07-857-4747 Thurs. thru Sun. 2 to 8 pm or call Director di Traci at 619-63
 2-2064. Pet Friendly:Dogs are welcome on approval/$10. Must take dogs with
  you. CABERNET COTTAGE is really cute for a couple or family. Grateful Dea
 d recorded Terrapin here. Jerry Garcia's favorite place to chill.Address: 
 20889 Geyserville Ave\, Geyserville\, CA 95441. Only 20 minutes from venue
 .\n\nHEALDSBURG: BEST WESTERN: Call \\(707\\) 433-0300 Address: 198 Dry Cr
 eek Rd\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448 Pet Friendly\n\nHOPLAND: THACTHER HOTEL: Ca
 ll  888-461-2017   Hotel Address: 13401 US-101\, Hopland\, CA 95449  Only 
 15 mins from venue.HOPLAND: STOCKFARM INN: Call 707-744-1977  Hotel Addres
 s:  13441 US-101\, Hopland\, CA 95449  Only 15 mins from venue.\n\nHotels 
 in Ukiah for better rates. Only 35 minutes from Ukiah via Hopland and Mpon
 tain House Road..\n\nTickets on Sale Now: Tell your friends!\n\n 
LOCATION:LE VIN WINERY aka Seawolf Wines
URL:https://www.caltix.com/e/davidnelson5?aff=cityspark
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bubbles & Bocce at Private Dry Creek Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T190000
UID:260420Oo7vOtHD7kGtahkVbk3A0g
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy an unforgettable afternoon of Bubbles & Bocce at the
  beautiful Healdsburg home of Chuck and Nancy Fry overlooking Dry Creek
  Valley! You’ll get to indulge in canapés\, pizza\, and special tre
 ats prepared by Jean-Pierre Moullé\, former executive chef of Berkley's 
 Chez Panisse. Jean-Pierre's work helped pioneer Chez Panisse as a leader i
 n the farm-to-table space—turning it into the Michelin-guide recognized\
 , world-renowned eatery it is today. He will be joined by Healdsburg's own
  Melissa and Sean McGaughey of Quail & Condor and Troubadour Bread & Bis
 tro\, who are known for crafting excellent French cuisine with Sonoma Cou
 nty ingredients.  Quail & Condor’s baked goods are highly acclaimed
 —as a 2025 James Beard Finalist and ranked by The New York Times as one 
 of the best bakeries in America. \n\nYour cornucopia of farm-to-table cui
 sine will be perfectly paired with sparkling wine from Hafner Vineyard—a
  three-generation Healdsburg Winery that has mastered the art of French wi
 nes. You’ll also be treated to refreshing Aperol Spritz\, and Champag
 ne. \n\nGather your friends to enjoy this special evening with bubbles\,
  a playful game of bocce\, and delicious food from some of the Sonoma Co
 unty’s best chefs. Don’t miss your chance to attend this lively\, f
 un-filled experience! \n\n**Our sincere gratitude to the Fry Family and H
 afner Vineyard for making this experience possible.** \n\n100% of proceeds
  from this event go to Boys & Girls Clubs of Sonoma-Marin. These funds sup
 port us in providing after-school programs\, summer camps\, and essential 
 resources for 11\,000 local youth—at Clubs from Geyserville to Petaluma.
  \n\n**Ticket sales for this event are live and close on Sunday\, April 2
 6th at 6pm.**
LOCATION:Boys & Girls Club of Sonoma-County
URL:https://hbginbloom2026.ggo.bid/n/package/15104467
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
UID:260312p-YbXytRDkuMCq8WeAItew
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Tasting Salon (Indoors Only)
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-brandlin-estate-win
 e-food-tasting-experience/18318441/2026-09-26T11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Live Music at Spicy Vines feat. 7 Acre Holler
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260206ufILJlqDFECktVK_2nZDIw
DESCRIPTION:*Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come 
 together.*\n\nJoin us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a ta
 sting room experience like no other — where top local musicians from acr
 oss the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll 
 and Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new so
 unds and new reasons to raise a glass. \n\n**7 Acre Holler** Acre Holleri
 s Sonoma County–based duo Cori Wood and Layne Bowen\, blending rich harm
 onies with Appalachian-inspired folk and Americana. \n\n**Details**\n\nNo
  cover. Walk-ins are welcome\, but this event tends to fill up quickly\, s
 o we recommend making a reservation. We are dog and family friendly!
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/event/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley of the Moon Vintage Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
UID:260904ojghtFRdlECuYI5o8jGkbg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Sonoma Valley's rich winemaking heritage at the  Val
 ley of the Moon Vintage Festival \, taking place September 24-27\, 2026. T
 his beloved community celebration features Sonoma Valley wines\, local foo
 d\, live music\, and family-friendly activities throughout the historic So
 noma Plaza.Highlights include the traditional Grape Stomp\, Blessing of th
 e Grapes\, live music\, a Wine Garden\, artisan fair\, kids' activities\, 
 and the Sonoma Valley Grand Tasting featuring wines from more than 40 wine
 ries. Special experiences throughout the weekend include a Harvest Immersi
 on\, Harvest Dinner\, and Brunch Bites & Bubbles. The 2026 festival celebr
 ates the 200th Anniversary of Sonoma Valley Wine with the theme "Year of C
 ommunity\," bringing locals and visitors together to celebrate harvest\, h
 istory\, wine\, and community.
LOCATION:Various Sonoma County Locations
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/the-valley-of-the-moon-vintage-festival/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:River & Redwoods Film Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T000000
UID:260713OwfmGGQp0EuI_yME9QeNrw
DESCRIPTION:The River & Redwoods Film Festival returns to Monte Rio for a 
 special weekend celebrating independent film\, creativity\, community\, an
 d the natural beauty of Northern California. Set among the towering redwoo
 ds and along the banks of the Russian River\, the festival brings filmmake
 rs\, film lovers\, artists\, and locals together for three unforgettable d
 ays of screenings\, conversations\, live events\, and connection. Hosted a
 t the historic Monte Rio Theater and neighboring venues in Monte Rio\, Cal
 ifornia\, River & Redwoods showcases narrative films\, documentaries\, sho
 rts\, student films\, and emerging voices from the Bay Area and beyond. Mo
 re than just a film festival\, River & Redwoods is about gathering in a be
 autiful small-town setting to experience great storytelling together. Expe
 ct filmmaker Q&As\, outdoor gatherings\, music\, local food and drink\, an
 d the laid-back creative spirit of Sonoma County. Whether you're an indust
 ry professional\, aspiring filmmaker\, or simply someone who loves movies 
 under the redwoods\, we invite you to spend the weekend with us.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/river-redwoods-film-festival/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Copperfield's Books Presents Kristin Hannah\, In Conversation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T193000
UID:260904qONRP4AxrUKxMumiL1Jsuw
DESCRIPTION:Kristin Hannah\, author of The Nightingale and The Four Winds\
 , comes to the LBC on Saturday\, September 26\, for a conversation about h
 er newest release\, The Women\, at once an intimate portrait of coming of 
 age in a dangerous time and an epic tale of a nation divided. Set in 1965\
 , it is a novel about deep friendships and bold patriotism\, a richly draw
 n story with a memorable heroine whose idealism and courage under fire wil
 l come to define an era. Join us for this warmhearted reading and conversa
 tion followed by a live audience Q&A. Presented by Copperfield's Books\, e
 very ticket includes a pre-signed paperback copy of the book\, The Women. 
 Photos and video are strictly prohibited for this event
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://lutherburbankcenter.org/event/kristin-hannah26/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
