BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Lantern Workshop - Weekend Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T160000
UID:260823aLETc-TCrE-XYWDOggNuJg
DESCRIPTION:Saturday & Sunday\n\nDate & Time\n\nSeptember 26 · 10:00 AM 
 – 5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 27 · 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 11
 0\n\nCategory\n\nEvents\, Fiber Arts\, Other\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Le
 vels\n\nAges\n\n18 and older\n\nOne Day Registration:\n\n$30\n\nFull Weeke
 nd Registration:\n\n$60\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$30 – $60\n\nJoin
  artist and educator\, Valerie Seaberg for a two-day immersive lantern-bui
 lding workshop inspired by Día de los Muertos\, ancestral remembrance\, a
 nd joy of creating in community. Together we will create illuminated lante
 rn sculptures that honor loved ones\, celebrate lineage from all cultures 
 and traditions\, and welcome the deepening beauty of fall and winter. Usin
 g willow\, bamboo\, reed\, paper\, and other sustainable materials\, parti
 cipants will learn how to build expressive sculptural lanterns from the in
 side out. Participants are encouraged to bring ideas\, sketches\, photogra
 phs\, symbols\, or meaningful inspiration connected to ancestors\, memory\
 , nature\, or personal vision. Lanterns may be abstract\, playful\, elegan
 t\, symbolic\, animal-inspired\, or devotional in form. This workshop is o
 pen to beginners as well as experienced makers.Together we will create a c
 elebration of light honoring those who came before us and illuminating the
  path forward.\n\nRequired Supply List\n\nPlease bring the following suppl
 ies to the class:\n\nPruning Shears\n\nSketchbook\n\nOptional: Meaningful 
 images\, poems\, or small materials to inspire your design
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/fall-lantern-workshop-weeke
 nd-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
