DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T210000
UID:260803B3a6xh-kgkmptFR7lrJosQ
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday · 6 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nAugust 18 – Septe
 mber 29\, 2026\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM No class September 8th\n\nLocation\n
 \nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\
 nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Fee:\n\
 n$200\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$230\n\nThis
  is a 6 week session with instructor\, Amy Hamley. This course is for stud
 ents interested in exploring both wheel throwing AND handbuilding\, and th
 e combination of both in one class! Learn from Hamley’s years of experti
 se in the field and enjoy creating handbuilt\, thrown\, and altered forms.
  Amy caters each syllabus closely to her group of students\, ensuring that
  every project fits the desires of participants. This course encourages fo
 lks to work on independent projects in the class\, receiving one on one su
 pport from Amy throughout the time. This course will include demos\, exerc
 ises\, and utilize a variety of methods to achieve the desired goal for ea
 ch student. Some projects may include wheel thrown vases with altered ador
 nments\, best practices for slump and hump molds\, and more.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/independent-projects-august
 /
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bill Frisell Harmony Five
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T193000
UID:2607216xDgE5gOuU6ZiwtmAk6_Fw
DESCRIPTION:Recognized as one of America’s 21 most vital and productive 
 performing artists\, Frisell was named an inaugural Doris Duke Artist in 2
 012. He is also a recipient of grants from United States Artists and Meet 
 the Composer\, among others. A singular stylist and influential artist wid
 ely considered one of the “big three” guitarists in jazz (along with J
 ohn Scofield and Pat Metheny)\, Frisell is a GRAMMY-winning musician and c
 omposer who served as one the SFJAZZ Center’s first five Resident Artist
 ic Directors in 2013-14. A veteran of over 40 albums as a leader with a st
 aggering history of collaborations with artists including Joe Lovano\, Elv
 is Costello\, John Zorn\, Lee Konitz\, Dave Douglas\, and Norah Jones.\n\n
 **Tuesday\, September 29\, 2026\, at 7:30 PM.** Doors at 6:30 PM.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/bill-frisell-harmony-five/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T183000
UID:260705yeAzTUUn502bkyFwX6JTdg
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-09-29T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260929T200000
UID:260704e_oD9BfIG0Sk6pG7uXqnQg
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 7:00 pm – 8:00 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/salsa-class-intermediate-tuesday/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
